The absmean ternary research direction builds on the BitNet family. The native
two-bit layout in tergon-math is a project definition, not an implementation of
GGUF TQ1_0/TQ2_0, I2_S, or TL kernels. It makes no lossless-FP-model claim.

Future Muon work must attribute Keller Jordan's original algorithm and relevant
scaling/distributed adaptations. No Muon implementation is included yet.
